  "regla": "Hundreds agree with the noun (doscientos pesos, doscientas personas); mil never changes and never takes un; millón takes un, has a plural (millones) and needs de before a noun. Un billón is a million millions: English billion is mil millones.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": null,
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Cien** = exactly 100: **cien pesos, cien mil**. From 101 on it's **ciento**: **ciento uno, ciento veinte**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Number",
            "Masculine",
            "Feminine"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "200",
              "doscientos",
              "doscientas"
            ],
            [
              "300",
              "trescientos",
              "trescientas"
            ],
            [
              "400",
              "cuatrocientos",
              "cuatrocientas"
            ],
            [
              "500",
              "quinientos",
              "quinientas"
            ],
            [
              "600",
              "seiscientos",
              "seiscientas"
            ],
            [
              "700",
              "setecientos",
              "setecientas"
            ],
            [
              "800",
              "ochocientos",
              "ochocientas"
            ],
            [
              "900",
              "novecientos",
              "novecientas"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Hundreds **agree** with the noun: **doscientos pesos, doscientas personas**. Watch the irregular ones: **quinientos, setecientos, novecientos**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Mil** never changes and never takes **un**: **mil, dos mil, diez mil**. **Miles de** = _thousands of_."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Millón** is a noun: **un millón, dos millones** (no accent in the plural). Before a noun add **de**: **un millón de pesos**. If more numbers follow, no **de**: **un millón quinientos mil pesos**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Number",
            "Spanish",
            "English"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "1,000,000",
              "un millón",
              "one million"
            ],
            [
              "1,000,000,000",
              "mil millones",
              "one billion"
            ],
            [
              "1,000,000,000,000",
              "un billón",
              "one trillion"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Careful: **un billón** is a **million millions**. English _billion_ is **mil millones**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Y** only goes between tens and units: **ciento treinta y dos, dos mil cuarenta y cinco**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Mexico writes numbers like English: **1,500** and **3.5**. Many Spanish-speaking countries swap the comma and the point."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: **cien** and **mil** go alone. **Millón** needs a buddy (**un**) and a bridge (**de**)."
        }
      ]
    },
